    {
      "id": "0873b1374542f736ef2f35ea5899fdd3a64c1855",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1956347037,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "As far as I can tell, the code was fine prior to your change #15863.\n\nTesting param_count twice seems a bit twisted to me. Could we simplify the code to something like below?\n\n```\n\t\tif (stmt_data != NULL) {\n\t\t\tguint64 param_count = stmt_data->param_metas.count;\n\t\t\tif ((conn_data->clnt_caps_ext & MYSQL_CAPS_QA)\n\t\t\t\t&& (exec_flags & MYSQL_PARAMETER_COUNT_AVAILABLE)) {\n\t\t\t\tguint8 lenfle = tvb_get_fle(tvb, req_tree, offset, &param_count, NULL);\n\t\t\t\tproto_tree_add_uint64(req_tree, hf_mysql_num_params, tvb, offset, lenfle, param_count);\n\t\t\t\toffset += lenfle;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif (param_count != 0) {\n\t\t\t\tguint8 stmt_bound;\n\t\t\t\toffset += (param_count + 7) / 8; /* NULL bitmap */\n\t\t\t\tproto_tree_add_item(req_tree, hf_mysql_new_parameter_bound_flag, tvb, offset, 1, ENC_NA);\n```\nOr can the param_count parameter be non zero when the (conn_data->clnt_caps_ext & MYSQL_CAPS_QA) && (exec_flags & MYSQL_PARAMETER_COUNT_AVAILABLE) is true?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
